From 121ac4c8889c4b116fcea44d5741c2801adc54e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:16:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] check: --config to select analyzers; attribute
 each event to its analyzer

rayhunter-check hardcoded AnalyzerConfig::default(), so offline re-analysis of a
capture ran only the default-on analyzers and could not exercise any detector
that is off by default (the v1.2.0 NAS detectors, or a future one). Add a
--config <file> flag that loads the [analyzers] table from a rayhunter config
(unknown keys ignored, so a full device config.toml works), threaded into the
pcap and qmdl analysis paths and the report metadata; without it the defaults
are unchanged.

Also record the producing analyzer's name on each event in the JSON report
(AnalysisRow::events is indexed by analyzer, so process_row labels each event by
position). This lets a consumer attribute a firing exactly, without matching on
message text, which the calibration snapshot relies on.

This makes false-positive calibration reproducible from committed code: a
capture can be re-scored with the detectors enabled (T-OR-113). Adds a toml
dependency to the check crate (already in the workspace lockfile via the daemon).
